Probability Distribution

The probability of a word is calculated as:

p(W = w) = C(w) / N

where:
C(w) = number of occurrences of word w
N = total number of words
(P(W=w) = probability of the word

For this example in the python code:
N=50

For example, the word programming occurs 5 times.

Therefore:

P(programming)= 5/50 =0.10

The word i occurs 11 times:

P(i)= 11/50 = 0.22


Bigram model

Mathematically, two consecutive words can be represented by random variables:

Wi,Wi+1 

A bigram is:

(Wi,Wi+1)

Conditional Probability

The main mathematical improvement is conditional probability.


P(w)

we ask:

What is the probability of seeing w, given the current word?

This is:
P(w|c)
 
where:

c = current word/context
w = next word

The bigram probability is estimated as:
P(w | c) = C(c, w)/C(c)

example -
The word I is followed by:

